[0.0, "o", "Investigating REAL data for tenant \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: can you check hubspot and tell me the closed won rate in the last 3 months?\r\n\u001b[2m2026-09-22 19:33:51\u001b[0m [\u001b[33m\u001b[1mwarning  \u001b[0m] \u001b[1mmcp.nothing_admissible        \u001b[0m \u001b[36mlabel\u001b[0m=\u001b[35mposthog\u001b[0m \u001b[36mreason\u001b[0m=\u001b[35m'the server was queried and offered no tool Cortex can admit; every tool must declare readOnlyHint: true'\u001b[0m\r\nRead-only: no write capability exists in the tool registry.\r\nCapabilities available to \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588: github, hubspot, posthog, slack\r\n  [  0.0s]          checking what data exists\r\n  [  6.8s]          found github__list_repositories\r\n  [  6.8s]          found posthog__list_events\r\n  [  6.8s]          found posthog__list_projects\r\n  [  6.8s]          checking memory for prior context\r\n  [ 11.0s] step 1   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 16.0s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 16.0s] step 1   calling hubspot__search\r\n  [ 16.0s] step 1   calling hubspot__closed_won\r\n  [ 18.0s] step 1   got hubspot__search (4 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 18.0s] step 1   got hubspot__search (5 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 18.0s] step 1   got hubspot__closed_won (6 observation(s) so far)\r\n  [ 18.0s] step 2   deciding what to look at\r\n  [ 39.6s]          drafting the report from 6 observation(s)\r\n  [ 53.6s]          checking every citation resolves\r\n  [ 53.6s]          re-reading each claim against its own evidence\r\n  sufficiency gate: skipped, this report asserts no cause (0.0s)\r\n  [ 62.0s]          writing the report\r\n\r\n==============================================================================\r\nQ: Can you check HubSpot and tell me the closed won rate in the last 3 months?\r\n==============================================================================\r\n\r\nConfidence: high\r\nTook 54s over 2 steps, 23,068 tokens, 6 observations gathered, 2 cited\r\n\r\nANSWER\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  The closed-won rate for the last \u2588 months (2026-06-22 to 2026-09-22) is about \u2588\u2588.\u2588% by deal count (\u2588 won out of \u2588\u2588 closed deals) and about \u2588\u2588.\u2588% by dollar value ($\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 won of $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 total closed).  [hubspot.search 3f6f5fac, hubspot.search ed5f79a9]\r\n\r\nFINDINGS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  Won vs. lost deal volume and value  (high)\r\n    - In the last \u2588 months, \u2588 deals closed won and \u2588\u2588 deals closed lost, a closed-won rate of about \u2588\u2588.\u2588% by count.  [hubspot.search 3f6f5fac, hubspot.search ed5f79a9]\r\n    - Closed-won deals totaled $\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 in amount versus $\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588,\u2588\u2588\u2588 for closed-lost deals over the same window, so the won rate by dollar value is lower still, about \u2588\u2588.\u2588% of the combined amount.  [hubspot.search 3f6f5fac, hubspot.search ed5f79a9]\r\n    - Several of the closed-won deals (e.g. \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588, \u2588\u2588\u2588\u2588) closed on the same date, 2026-06-30, and have no recorded source, contacts, or deal_type, suggesting they may be legacy/import records rather than deals worked in this period.  [hubspot.search 3f6f5fac]\r\n\r\nRISKS AND CAVEATS\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - \u2588\u2588 closed-lost rows were retrieved but only summarized via a digest, not individually read; the rate calculation relies on the digest's aggregate count (\u2588\u2588) rather than inspecting each row, so any anomaly in individual records (duplicates, wrong close dates) would not be caught.\r\n  - \u2588 of the \u2588 closed-won deals share an identical close_date of 2026-06-30 and lack source/contact data, which may indicate bulk-imported or backdated records rather than deals genuinely closed in this \u2588-month window.\r\n\r\nDATA QUALITY\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  - Closed-lost figures were read only as a computed digest (counts, ranges, clusters) over all \u2588\u2588 rows, not as individual records; the digest is trusted for aggregate stats used here.\r\n  - The github commits sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github deployments sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github issues sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The github links sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog annotations sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n  - The posthog events sync last succeeded \u2588\u2588 days ago. Stored history for it is that old, and a recent change may not appear.\r\n\r\nSOURCES\r\n------------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n  3f6f5fac  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-06-22..2026-09-22&hs_is_closed_won=true\r\n  ed5f79a9  hubspot.search  hubspot://crm/v3/objects/deals/search?closedate=2026-06-22..2026-09-22&hs_is_closed_lost=true\r\n\r\nphase breakdown (62s wall, 59s measured)\r\n  phase        calls  seconds  share    mean  tokens\r\n  survey           1      6.8   11%     6.8  in 0 out 0\r\n  recall           1      4.1 